.TH APT-DIFF 1 "2026-10-28" "apt-diff 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
apt\-diff \- snapshot dpkg packages, /etc, systemd units and listening ports; audit what changed
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B apt-diff
.RI [ \-\-store DIR ]
.RI [ \-\-root DIR ]
.RI [ \-\-json ]
.RI [ \-\-no-color ]
.RI [ \-q ]
.I COMMAND
.RI [ args ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B apt-diff
captures the state of a Debian or Raspberry Pi OS system into compressed
snapshots and diffs them over time.  Each snapshot records:
.TP
\(bu every installed dpkg package with version, architecture and status
.TP
\(bu a SHA-256 hash of every regular file under
.I /etc
plus symlink targets and permissions
.TP
\(bu systemd unit files and their enablement (via
.BR systemctl (1)
when available)
.TP
\(bu listening TCP ports parsed from
.IR /proc/net/tcp[6]
.TP
\(bu kernel version, OS release and hostname
.PP
Snapshots are plain gzip-JSON and need no privileges to read.  A snapshot
of a typical desktop system is well under 1 MB.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init
Take the first snapshot and mark it as the baseline.  This is the reference
that
.B check
compares against.
.TP
.B snapshot
Take a new snapshot and prune old ones (default retention: 30).
.TP
.BI diff " \fR[\fIold\fR] \fR[\fInew\fR]"
Compare two snapshots.  Defaults: baseline (or previous) vs latest.
Snapshot arguments may be
.IR latest ,
.IR baseline ,
a timestamp such as
.IR 20261028T120000 ,
a file name, or a path.
.TP
.B check
Diff latest against baseline.  Prints nothing and exits 0 when unchanged;
prints a summary and exits 1 when anything changed.  Designed for cron and
CI.
.TP
.B log
List snapshots (newest first) with change counts between consecutive ones.
.TP
.BI show " \fR[\fIname\fR]"
Print a one-page summary of a snapshot (default: latest).
.TP
.BI prune " \-\-keep N"
Delete all but the newest N snapshots.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-store " DIR"
Snapshot directory (default
.I /var/lib/apt-diff
as root, else
.IR ~/.local/share/apt-diff ).
.TP
.BI \-\-root " DIR"
Inspect a different system root (chroots, test fixtures).
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit machine-readable JSON (diff, check, log).
.TP
.B \-\-no-color
Disable ANSI colors.
.TP
.B \-q, \-\-quiet
Quiet output.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B check
returns 0 when the system matches the baseline and 1 when it does not;
2 on usage errors.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Set up nightly snapshots and get mail-like warnings:
.PP
.nf
  sudo apt-diff init
  echo "0 3 * * * root apt-diff check -q" > /etc/cron.d/apt-diff
.fi
.PP
What changed since the last snapshot?
.PP
.nf
  apt-diff snapshot && apt-diff diff
.fi
.PP
Find the snapshot right before things broke, then inspect it:
.PP
.nf
  apt-diff log
  apt-diff diff 20261028T030000
  apt-diff show 20261028T030000
.fi
.PP
Audit a Raspberry Pi from your workstation (no install needed):
.PP
.nf
  make zipapp && scp dist/apt-diff pi@raspberrypi:
  ssh pi@raspberrypi ./apt-diff init
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/apt-diff
Default snapshot store (root).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/apt-diff
Default snapshot store (unprivileged users).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dpkg (1),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR etckeeper (1)
.SH BUGS
The version comparator approximates dpkg ordering; it handles epochs,
numeric runs and the tilde rule, which covers practical cases.
Permission-unreadable files (e.g.
.IR /etc/ssl/private
when unprivileged) are recorded with an empty hash; that only ever
produces one benign "modified" entry if permissions change.
